  30:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c **** 
  31:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c **** /**
  32:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * @ingroup groupFilters
  33:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  */
  34:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c **** 
  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * @defgroup FIR_Lattice Finite Impulse Response (FIR) Lattice Filters
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * This set of functions implements Finite Impulse Response (FIR) lattice filters
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * for Q15, Q31 and floating-point data types.  Lattice filters are used in a
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * variety of adaptive filter applications.  The filter structure is feedforward and
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * the net impulse response is finite length.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * The functions operate on blocks
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * of input and output data and each call to the function processes
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <code>blockSize</code> samples through the filter.  <code>pSrc</code> and
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <code>pDst</code> point to input and output arrays containing <code>blockSize</code> values.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par Algorithm:
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \image html FIRLattice.gif "Finite Impulse Response Lattice filter"
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * The following difference equation is implemented:
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *    f0[n] = g0[n] = x[n]
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *    fm[n] = fm-1[n] + km * gm-1[n-1] for m = 1, 2, ...M
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *    gm[n] = km * fm-1[n] + gm-1[n-1] for m = 1, 2, ...M
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *    y[n] = fM[n]
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <code>pCoeffs</code> points to tha array of reflection coefficients of size <code>numStages</cod
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * Reflection Coefficients are stored in the following order.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *    {k1, k2, ..., kM}
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * where M is number of stages
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <code>pState</code> points to a state array of size <code>numStages</code>.
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * The state variables (g values) hold previous inputs and are stored in the following order.
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *    {g0[n], g1[n], g2[n] ...gM-1[n]}
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * The state variables are updated after each block of data is processed; the coefficients are unto
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par Instance Structure
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * The coefficients and state variables for a filter are stored together in an instance data struct
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * A separate instance structure must be defined for each filter.
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * Coefficient arrays may be shared among several instances while state variable arrays cannot be s
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * There are separate instance structure declarations for each of the 3 supported data types.
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par Initialization Functions
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * There is also an associated initialization function for each data type.
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * The initialization function performs the following operations:
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * - Zeros out the values in the state buffer.
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * To do this manually without calling the init function, assign the follow subfields of the instan
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * numStages, pCoeffs, pState. Also set all of the values in pState to zero.
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par
  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * Use of the initialization function is optional.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccNbXdQ2.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure cannot be placed in
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * To place an instance structure into a const data section, the instance structure must be manuall
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * Set the values in the state buffer to zeros and then manually initialize the instance structure 
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *arm_fir_lattice_instance_f32 S = {numStages, pState, pCoeffs};
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *arm_fir_lattice_instance_q31 S = {numStages, pState, pCoeffs};
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  *arm_fir_lattice_instance_q15 S = {numStages, pState, pCoeffs};
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par
  96:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * where <code>numStages</code> is the number of stages in the filter; <code>pState</code> is the a
  97:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * <code>pCoeffs</code> is the address of the coefficient buffer.
  98:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * \par Fixed-Point Behavior
  99:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * Care must be taken when using the fixed-point versions of the FIR Lattice filter functions.
 100:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * In particular, the overflow and saturation behavior of the accumulator used in each function mus
 101:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  * Refer to the function specific documentation below for usage guidelines.
 102:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_lattice_f32.c ****  */
